  "task": {
    "objective": "Guide all six sheep through timed fence gates into their matching upper or lower pen using combined spatial pressure and temporary calls.",
    "natural_termination": "Every sheep enters either pen, preserving correct and wrong admissions separately; otherwise truncate at 96 nonterminal steps.",
    "interaction": "All shepherds' bounded repulsion and call attraction add into the actual cell field. A teammate can reinforce or cancel another's intended pressure, change flock crowding, or consume a gate-opening opportunity. Rest, pressure, call and gate operation compete for time and energy. Gatekeepers help other roles' target flocks at the expense of steering their own.",
    "observation_access": "All entity positions and declared attributes are public. Role identity is self information. Fixed maps, constant labels and redundant derived geometry add no hidden information. Only native observations and legal masks enter a learner."
  },
